00:21:00.910 --> 00:21:04.330
So why should you endure that?

00:21:04.330 --> 00:21:05.480
Why should you do it?

00:21:05.480 --> 00:21:07.930
I think this class
is really for people

00:21:07.930 --> 00:21:11.290
who have this obsessive
need to understand

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:15.830
how things work, all the way
down to the atom, so to speak.

00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:19.490
And I think when you
get through this class,

00:21:19.490 --> 00:21:21.190
I think you will have
really leveled up

00:21:21.190 --> 00:21:23.240
in terms of your
research, engineering,

00:21:23.240 --> 00:21:24.970
and the level of
comfort that you'll

00:21:24.970 --> 00:21:29.160
have in building ML systems at
scale will just be, I think,

00:21:29.160 --> 00:21:31.110
something.

00:21:31.110 --> 00:21:33.210
There's also a bunch
of reasons that you

00:21:33.210 --> 00:21:34.840
shouldn't take the class.

00:21:34.840 --> 00:21:38.650
For example, if you want to get
any research done this quarter,

00:21:38.650 --> 00:21:40.810
maybe this class isn't for you.

00:21:40.810 --> 00:21:44.040
If you're interested in
learning just about the hottest

00:21:44.040 --> 00:21:47.280
new techniques, there
are many other classes

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:49.350
that can probably
deliver on that

00:21:49.350 --> 00:21:52.350
better than, for
example, you spending

00:21:52.350 --> 00:21:55.410
a lot of time debugging BPE.

00:21:55.410 --> 00:21:58.020
And this is really,
I think, a class

00:21:58.020 --> 00:22:01.920
about the primitives and
learning things bottom

00:22:01.920 --> 00:22:06.570
up as opposed to the latest.

00:22:06.570 --> 00:22:10.380
And also if you're interested
in building language models

00:22:10.380 --> 00:22:17.880
or forex, this is probably not
the first class you would take.

00:22:17.880 --> 00:22:21.690
I think, practically
speaking, as much

00:22:21.690 --> 00:22:24.550
as I made fun of prompting,
prompting is great.

00:22:24.550 --> 00:22:25.530
Fine tuning is great.

00:22:25.530 --> 00:22:28.320
If you can do that
and it works, then I

00:22:28.320 --> 00:22:31.330
think that is something you
should absolutely start with.

00:22:31.330 --> 00:22:34.350
So I don't want people
taking this class

00:22:34.350 --> 00:22:37.260
and thinking that, great,
any problem, the first step

00:22:37.260 --> 00:22:39.400
is to train a language
model from scratch.

00:22:39.400 --> 00:22:44.070
That is not the right
way of thinking about it.

00:22:44.070 --> 00:22:44.954
