00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:25.840
OK, so the class has
five assignments.

00:23:25.840 --> 00:23:31.360
And each of the assignments, we
don't provide scaffolding code.

00:23:31.360 --> 00:23:34.930
In the sense that
literally giving you

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:39.370
a blank file and you're
supposed to build things up.

00:23:39.370 --> 00:23:43.690
And in the spirit of
building from scratch.

00:23:43.690 --> 00:23:46.060
But we're not that mean.

00:23:46.060 --> 00:23:48.910
We do provide unit tests
and some adapter interfaces

00:23:48.910 --> 00:23:53.600
that allow you to check
correctness of different pieces.

00:23:53.600 --> 00:23:55.310
And also the
assignment write-up,

00:23:55.310 --> 00:23:57.130
if you walk through
it, does do it

00:23:57.130 --> 00:23:59.300
for a gentle job of doing that.

00:23:59.300 --> 00:24:04.240
But you are on your own for
making good software design

00:24:04.240 --> 00:24:06.610
decisions and figuring out
what you name your functions

00:24:06.610 --> 00:24:08.600
and how to organize your code.

00:24:08.600 --> 00:24:13.180
Which is a useful
skill, I think.

00:24:13.180 --> 00:24:16.270
So one strategy I think,
for all assignments

00:24:16.270 --> 00:24:17.990
is that there is a
piece of assignment,

00:24:17.990 --> 00:24:21.490
which is just implement
the thing and make sure

00:24:21.490 --> 00:24:22.160
it's correct.

00:24:22.160 --> 00:24:26.130
That mostly you can do
locally on your laptop.

00:24:26.130 --> 00:24:27.690
You shouldn't need
compute for that.

00:24:27.690 --> 00:24:31.130
And then we have
a cluster that you

00:24:31.130 --> 00:24:35.240
can run for benchmarking
both accuracy and speed.

00:24:35.240 --> 00:24:37.760
Right, so I want
everyone to embrace

00:24:37.760 --> 00:24:42.330
this idea of that you want
to use a small data set

00:24:42.330 --> 00:24:45.380
or as few resources as
possible to prototype

00:24:45.380 --> 00:24:47.140
before running large jobs.

00:24:47.140 --> 00:24:49.640
You shouldn't be debugging with
one billion parameter models

00:24:49.640 --> 00:24:52.970
on the cluster if
you can help it.

00:24:52.970 --> 00:24:54.950
OK.

00:24:54.950 --> 00:24:59.990
There's some assignments which
